%abc-2.1
% Melody, chords and words transcribed by hand from the writers' own lead sheet,
% sources/sheetPdf.pdf (songsofpraise.org/pdf/fill.pdf), bar for bar. Bar numbers
% match the PDF. The piano left hand and the inner voices are not transcribed.
% Checked against the melody track of sources/tune.mid (tools/check-abc-midi.py).
% Where the two differ the PDF wins. In verse 3 the MIDI sings "my life I owe" with
% "I" on C#5 an eighth early, where the PDF has F#4 on beat 4; sings "One who saves"
% with "who" on C#5 on beat 4, where the PDF has A4 on the and of 3; and moves "to"
% ("Lord, to You") and "is" ("that is why") by an eighth. The MIDI's first melody
% note is in its bar 9; the PDF's intro is seven bars, so the voice enters in bar 8.
X:1
T:Come Fill My Heart
C:Music by Elton Smith
C:Words by Elton Smith, Larry Holder and Steve Israel
Z:Transcribed from the writers' lead sheet (2000)
M:4/4
L:1/8
K:G
